The attached image, Figure 6 from the npj Vaccines 2017 paper, illustrates Nano-11's role in improving antigen targeting and retention. Panel a shows flow cytometry histograms of CD86 expression on different OVA+ myeloid cell types in draining lymph nodes, with MigDCs exhibiting the highest expression, indicating their potent APC function. Panel b further phenotypes OVA+ and OVA- MigDCs based on CD11b and Ly6C markers, revealing that Nano-11 preferentially targets specific MigDC subsets, predominantly CD11b+ DCs and MoDCs, for OVA delivery. Panel c, a whole-mouse imaging series, demonstrates that Nano-11, similar to aluminum hydroxide, significantly prolongs Alexa Fluor 647-labeled OVA retention at the injection site compared to soluble OVA, ensuring sustained antigen availability.